{
  "description": "What one agent may read (spec 6.11, 12.1.4): one rule for alp_inbox, alp_thread and alp_ack. A received message (direction in) is visible if it is addressed to the person or to this agent (to_delegate), isn't held (or its held_until has passed), and the agent meets its delivery constraints with the client terms recorded for it. A sent message (direction out) is visible only to the agent that sent it (from_delegate), or to every agent when the broker sent it for the person (no from_delegate). A reader's since is when its binding started (spec 5.4): a received message addressed to it is visible only if its broker received it (stored_at) at or after since, and a message it sent only if its broker signed it (created_at) at or after since, so an agent that takes a disconnected agent's label reads nothing of the earlier agent's. A sent message's record may be stored after the binding started (it is stored once the receipt is back); its created_at decides. expected.visible lists the visible ids in order.",
  "now": "2026-11-09T14:00:00Z",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a business agent reads a constrained reply; a consumer agent of the same person doesn't (thread, inbox and ack alike)",
      "reader": {
        "delegate": "alp:ana@example.org/agent-a",
        "attestation": "vendor",
        "class": "business",
        "client": {
          "no_training": true,
          "retention_days": 30
        }
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "id": "01M7069S40GJCVZD54FN7WASVA",
          "status": "delivered",
          "direction": "in",
          "constraints": {
            "deliver_to": {
              "min_class": "business"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "visible": [
          "01M7069S40GJCVZD54FN7WASVA"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
